{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO & JCO no-fault eviction relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord ending a tenancy for a no-fault reason in an RSO- or JCO-covered unit must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD before serving notice and pay relocation assistance within 15 days.","key_value":"$11,000–$14,400 eligible; $23,150–$27,400 qualified per unit, 7/1/2026–6/30/2027","coverage_conditions":"Units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO); relocation assistance is paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Amount and eligibility depend on the tenant's length of tenancy and income and whether the tenant is 62+, disabled, or has minor dependent children.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Replacing a resident manager with another; natural-disaster hazardous conditions not caused by landlord negligence. Landlord may offset accumulated rent except for government orders to vacate. 'Mom and Pop' reduced payments apply for owner/family occupancy in buildings of four or fewer units under LAMC 151.30.","penalty":"Failure to file the Landlord Declaration with LAHD makes the eviction a violation of the RSO or JCO; a tenant may raise non-payment of relocation assistance as an affirmative defense.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","valid_through":"2027-06-30","citation":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §151.00 et seq.); Los Angeles Just Cause Ordinance (L.A.M.C. §165.00 et seq.)","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":"Relocation must comply with the state Housing Crisis Act or city laws, whichever is higher; RSO/JCO amounts are enhanced for lower income tenants under the HCA or RPO.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance relocation requirements","requirement":"An owner who demolishes a Protected Unit for new construction within 5 years after filing the notice must provide RPO relocation, choosing one of three options, and pay the highest applicable state or city amount.","key_value":"penalty from $250,000 per displaced unit; three relocation options","coverage_conditions":"Applies only to Protected Units demolished for the purpose of new construction; Protected Units include all RSO units and units rent-controlled or rented to lower income households within the past five years.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","role":"covered","text":"only Protected Units demolished for the purpose of new construction"}],"per_tenancy":"Enhanced relocation applies to lower income tenants (80% AMI or lower); other tenants get regular RSO or JCO amounts.","coverage_quotes":["The RPO only applies to Protected Units that will be demolished for the purpose of new construction."]},"exemptions":"Protected Units not occupied by a lower income tenant, and units that are not Protected Units, follow the regular RSO or JCO relocation rules instead.","penalty":"Financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","effective_date":"2025-02-11","valid_through":null,"citation":"Ordinances Nos. 188481 and 188482","quoted_span":"Owners who demolish a Protected Unit for the purpose of new construction within 5 years after the filing of the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD are required to comply with relocation requirements under the RPO. Failure to comply with the RPO may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","interaction":"Owners must pay the highest of the applicable relocation amounts to comply with State and City laws; the RPO codified and expanded upon the state Housing Crisis Act.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Housing Crisis Act relocation for lower-income demolition","requirement":"Under the state Housing Crisis Act, only lower income households (80% AMI or lower) displaced by demolition for new construction receive relocation payment consistent with the benefits public entities must pay under Government Code Chapter 16.","key_value":"relocation benefits per Gov. Code Ch. 16; households at 80% AMI or lower","coverage_conditions":"Lower income households (80% AMI or lower) displaced for demolition where the owner will replace the units with new construction.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies to lower income tenants displaced for demolition for new construction; RSO/JCO amounts must be enhanced for these tenants regardless of the RPO.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Cal. Gov. Code §66300","quoted_span":"The City’s Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO) and the State’s Housing Crisis Act (HCA) require that ONLY lower income households (80% AMI or lower) being displaced for demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction receive relocation payment consistent to the relocation benefits required to be paid by public entities under Chapter 16 (commencing with Section 7260) of Division 7 of Title 1 (Government Code 66300.6(b)(4)(A)).","interaction":"The HCA sets a state floor; city RSO/JCO amounts must be enhanced for lower income tenants under the HCA regardless of whether the RPO applies.","relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

